Description:

A Sieve notify :message template that references "$text[" is now rejected
when the script is compiled, and is emitted literally rather than expanded if
it is encountered at run time.  The reference must give a non-zero decimal
length and close with "]$", and using it at all now requires the "body"
extension.  Previously the length was read by scanning forward without
checking that a closing bracket was present, so a truncated reference read
past the end of the message body and could place unrelated server memory into
the notification that was sent.

Tracked as GitHub security advisory GHSA-gq3h-f75f-hrj9.


